    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What applications benefit from this skill?",
        "answer": "It supports AI chat interfaces that need progress feedback, interactive state updates, or synchronized thread behavior."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does this skill create a complete chat application?",
        "answer": "No. It adds streaming patterns to an existing ChatKit frontend and compatible backend."
      },
      {
        "question": "How should errors affect locked interface controls?",
        "answer": "The error handler should clear response state, unlock controls, and show a user-friendly message."
      },
      {
        "question": "When should I use a client effect?",
        "answer": "Use a client effect for one-way interface updates that do not require a returned value."
      },
      {
        "question": "When should I use a client tool?",
        "answer": "Use a client tool when the assistant needs a limited, validated result from browser state."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does the skill include security controls?",
        "answer": "It does not provide complete controls. Applications must validate payloads, restrict tool names, and minimize returned client data."
